        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=0.6$; the cost increases by £0.60 per mile.",
          "worked": "Using $(1,3)$ and $(6,6)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\frac{\\text{change in cost}}{\\text{change in miles}}\\\\m&=\\frac{6-3}{6-1}\\\\m&=\\frac{3}{5}\\\\m&=0.6\\end{align*}$$\nThe cost increases by £0.60 for each additional mile travelled.",
